static.solution:
\vec{OP}=\left\lt 5,5,0\right> and \vec{OQ}=\left\lt 0,5,2\right>. Thus,



S=\frac{1}{2} || \vec{OP} \times \vec{OQ} ||



We compute the cross product:



\vec{OP} \times \vec{OQ}=
\left| \begin{array}{ccc}
 \boldsymbol{i} \amp  \boldsymbol{j} \amp  \boldsymbol{k} \\
 5 \amp  5 \amp  0 \\
 0 \amp  5 \amp  2
\end{array} \right|
= 
  \left| \begin{array}{cc} 5 \amp  0 \\ 5 \amp  2 \end{array} \right| \boldsymbol{i}
- \left| \begin{array}{cc} 5 \amp  0 \\ 0 \amp  2 \end{array} \right| \boldsymbol{j}
+ \left| \begin{array}{cc} 5 \amp  5 \\ 0 \amp  5 \end{array} \right| \boldsymbol{k} 


\qquad = 10 \boldsymbol{i}  - 10 \boldsymbol{j} + 25 \boldsymbol{k}



S=\frac{1}{2}|| 10 \boldsymbol{i}  - 10 \boldsymbol{j} + 25 \boldsymbol{k} ||
   =\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{(10)^2+(-10)^2+(25)^2}
   \approx 14.3614.
